## At work

High cholesterol does not usually affect your ability to work. You may need time off for blood tests or appointments. Many workplaces offer health checks.

## Is it a disability?

High cholesterol on its own is **unlikely** to count as a disability under the Equality Act, because it does not usually affect daily activities. Conditions it can lead to, such as coronary heart disease or stroke, may count.

## Benefits

Disability benefits such as PIP are based on how a condition affects your daily life, so high cholesterol alone will not usually qualify. If you also have heart disease, a stroke or another condition, read about those:

- [Coronary heart disease](/conditions/heart-and-circulation/coronary-heart-disease/)
- [Stroke](/conditions/heart-and-circulation/stroke/)
- [Peripheral arterial disease](/conditions/heart-and-circulation/peripheral-arterial-disease/)

## Prescriptions

Statins are usually taken for life. In England, a **prescription prepayment certificate** can save money if you pay for 2 or more items a month. Prescriptions are **free in Wales**. Check if you could get free prescriptions with our [NHS health costs check](/support/health-costs/checker/).
